    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something I can’t ignore but also find fascinating when broken down into manageable parts. It’s not intimidating for me; it’s more of a toolkit for understanding patterns, whether in art, economics, or even knitting measurements. My parents taught me early that logic is universal, so I approach it with curiosity rather than fear.",
